# Plugin Composition

`umo-agentic-core` owns lifecycle invariants. Other plugins may specialize
behavior, but must compose through explicit ownership and delegation.

Rules:

- Non-core plugins must declare `dependsOn: ["umo-agentic-core"]`.
- Non-core plugins must delegate lifecycle, memory, planning, quality, review,
  and closeout concerns to `umo-agentic-core`.
- Planning phase semantics and beads are core responsibilities in v1. There is
  no separate planning plugin.
- A plugin may strengthen a core invariant, but cannot weaken, replace, or fork it.
- Duplicate ownership of the same surface fails validation until one plugin delegates.
- Generated reports and artifacts must record active plugin names and versions.
